    "faq1Title": "What is free, and how are service fees explained?",
    "faq1Text": "Initial advice and background assessment are free. Any paid follow-up will be explained before you decide. Tuition, tests, translations and visa charges are separate third-party costs and need confirmation.",
    "faq2Title": "When should I start preparing?",
    "faq2Text": "Start with your intended intake, then work back from university and scholarship deadlines. Plan tests and documents around those dates. Dates vary; requirements for a future cycle may not yet be published.",
    "faq3Title": "Can a Myanmar high school graduate apply directly for a bachelor’s degree?",
    "faq3Text": "It depends on the country, university, programme and qualification system. Matriculation, Chinese-school diplomas, GED and A-Level are not automatically equivalent. A foundation course or additional tests may be needed; the university confirms recognition.",
    "faq4Title": "Which documents should I prepare?",
    "faq4Text": "Common documents include a graduation or expected-graduation certificate, full transcripts, passport and language evidence. Translations, references, personal statements, financial or guardianship documents and portfolios depend on your application.",
    "faq5Title": "Can I ask for advice before taking HSK or IELTS?",
    "faq5Text": "Yes. Test types, scores, component minima and validity vary by programme; exemptions cannot be assumed. Select only results you already have. Missing evidence remains a gap or a point to verify.",
    "faq6Title": "Which scholarships can I explore?",
    "faq6Text": "Explore official scholarship sources, coverage, dates and obligations by destination and university. Check application conditions against your nationality, qualifications, grades and programme; each listing shows its review status.",
    "faq7Title": "What does passport and student visa guidance cover?",
    "faq7Text": "We help organise the official process, document checklist and preparation order. Visa and residence rules differ by destination. Check current authority and embassy rules when applying; approval is their decision.",
    "faq8Title": "Are my scores saved or sent anywhere?",
    "faq8Text": "Matching takes place in your browser without automatic uploads. “Save on this device” stores a local copy only when selected; you control exported files. Opening Messenger does not attach your scores. You choose what to share.",
